ng that hysterectomy is part of a broader set of non–fertility-sparing strategies rather than an isolated intervention. [Data: Entities (4863, 2187); Relationships (10616)]\"},{\"summary\":\"Key patient-impact considerations include fertility loss and ovarian preservation vs removal\",\"explanation\":\"The hysterectomy entity description states that hysterectomy permanently eliminates the ability to carry a pregnancy in the uterus, establishing a major life impact and aligning with its placement under non–fertility-sparing management options. [Data: Entities (2187, 4863); Relationships (10616, 3756)]\\n\\nIt also notes that ovaries may be removed or preserved during hysterectomy: removal causes surgical (premature) menopause, whereas preservation may allow continued ovarian hormonal function. Although ovaries are not separate entities in this dataset, these statements describe significant downstream physiological and quality-of-life implications associated with hysterectomy-based care. [Data: Entities (2187)]\"}],\"rating\":3.2,\"rating_explanation\":\"The impact severity is low-to-moderate because the community describes standard clinical procedures and decision pathways with significant patient implications but no evidence of illegality, malicious activity, or broader societal harm within the provided data. [Data: Entities (2187, 2188, 4863)]\"}", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, "provider_specific_fields": {"native_finish_reason": "stop"}}], "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1491, "prompt_tokens": 3057, "total_tokens": 4548, "completion_tokens_details": {"accepted_prediction_tokens": null, "audio_tokens": null, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "rejected_prediction_tokens": null, "text_tokens": null}, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 1536, "text_tokens": null, "image_tokens": null}}, "service_tier": null}}}